[21.051175, "o", "> "]
[21.051334, "o", "2. **Parse and Format Dates**: Convert the '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"' ISO 8601 timestamp into a date string in the format '\"'\"'YYYY-MM-DD'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.051351, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.051385, "o", "3. **Extract and Rename Fields**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.051395, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.051404, "o", "> "]
[21.051461, "o", "   - Extract '\"'\"'id'\"'\"' as '\"'\"'user_id'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.051471, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.051518, "o", "   - Extract '\"'\"'username'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.05153, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.051568, "o", "   - Extract '\"'\"'email'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.051581, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.051635, "o", "   - Extract and format '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.051647, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.051721, "o", "   - Extract the count of roles as '\"'\"'role_count'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.051731, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.051877, "o", "   - Extract the first role from the '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' array as '\"'\"'primary_role'\"'\"' (if roles exist, otherwise null).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.051888, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.051896, "o", "> "]
[21.052027, "o", "4. **Sort Users**: Sort the resulting users alphabetically by their '\"'\"'username'\"'\"' in ascending order.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.052039, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.052168, "o", "5. **Output Format**: The output must be a JSON array of objects formatted with indentation of 2 spaces.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.052178, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.052186, "o", "> "]
[21.052448, "o", "6. **Save Command**: Save the exact jq command you execute to a file named '\"'\"'/app/cmd.sh'\"'\"'. This file should contain the complete jq command used to generate the output, including all options and arguments.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.052465, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.052471, "o", "> "]
[21.052671, "o", "7. **Save Arguments**: Save all jq arguments(excluding input/output files) to a YAML file named '\"'\"'/app/jq_args.yaml'\"'\"'. This file should contain exactly two keys:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.052688, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.052773, "o", "> "]
[21.052781, "o", "   - '\"'\"'filter'\"'\"': A string containing the jq filter expression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.052847, "o", "   - '\"'\"'args'\"'\"': A list of strings, each representing a complete jq argument including both flags and values\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.052854, "o", ">    \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.052896, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.052927, "o", "   '\"'\"'/app/jq_args.yaml'\"'\"' Example format:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.052939, "o", "   ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.05297, "o", "   filter: \"group_by(.address.city)\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.052991, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053014, "o", "   args:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053035, "o", "     - \"--unbuffered\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053061, "o", "     - \"--argjson min_count 5\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.053087, "o", "> "]
[21.053107, "o", "     - \"--tab\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>    ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053132, "o", "   \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053197, "o", "   '\"'\"'/app/jq_args.yaml'\"'\"' will be used to construct and execute a single jq command as follows:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.053223, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053329, "o", "   `jq $(yq -r '\"'\"'.args[]'\"'\"' /app/jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '\"'\"'.filter'\"'\"' /app/jq_args.yaml)\" /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json`\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.053351, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053377, "o", "   \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053402, "o", "   For the example above, the constructed command would be:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.05343, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053521, "o", "   `jq --unbuffered --argjson min_count 5 --tab '\"'\"'group_by(.address.city)'\"'\"' /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json`\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.053547, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.053576, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>    This means:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.053602, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053632, "o", "   1. All arguments in the '\"'\"'args'\"'\"' list will be passed directly to jq\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.05365, "o", "> "]
[21.053709, "o", "   2. The filter string will be passed as the jq filter expression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053775, "o", "   3. The input file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' is fixed and will be used as input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.053798, "o", "> "]
[21.053848, "o", "   4. The output will be redirected to '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.053877, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053917, "o", "   5. jq will be executed exactly once with all these components\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.053943, "o", ">    \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.053967, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.053988, "o", "   Requirements for the YAML file:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.054103, "o", "   - The '\"'\"'args'\"'\"' list should contain complete jq arguments, with both flags and their values (if any)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.054177, "o", "   - Each argument should be a separate string in the list\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.054226, "o", "   - For flag-only arguments, include just the flag (e.g., '\"'\"'--unbuffered'\"'\"', '\"'\"'--tab'\"'\"')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.054249, "o", "> "]
[21.054338, "o", "   - For arguments with values, include both the flag and value as a single string (e.g., '\"'\"'--argjson min_count 5'\"'\"')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.054359, "o", "> "]
[21.054447, "o", "   - Do not include the jq command itself, the filter expression, or file paths in the args list\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.05458, "o", "   - File paths other than the required input file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' and output redirections should not appear in the args\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.054646, "o", "   - The filter should be a single string containing the complete jq filter expression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.054679, "o", "> "]
[21.054897, "o", "**Note on examples below**: In the following Data Schema sections, all content following the '\"'\"'#'\"'\"' symbol is just explanatory commentary and will NOT appear in the actual JSON files. These comments are only provided to clarify the structure and requirements.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.054934, "o", "> **Input Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.055019, "o", "The input JSON file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' is an array of user objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.055055, "o", "[\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.05511, "o", "    \"id\": 1,                  # Unique numeric identifier for the user\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.055134, "o", "> "]
[21.055178, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",   # User'\"'\"'s unique username (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.055202, "o", "> "]
[21.055248, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # User'\"'\"'s email address (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.055273, "o", "> "]
[21.05533, "o", "    \"status\": \"active\",       # User status: '\"'\"'active'\"'\"' or '\"'\"'inactive'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.055354, "o", "> "]
[21.055418, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02T20:59:10.109812Z\",  # ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC) of the last login\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.055442, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.055503, "o", "    \"roles\": [\"admin\", \"editor\"]  # Array of roles assigned to the user (may be empty)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.055526, "o", ">   },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.055555, "o", "  ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.055583, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.055604, "o", "**Output Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.0557, "o", "The output JSON file '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"' must be an array of objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.055725, "o", "> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.055747, "o", "> "]
[21.055797, "o", "    \"user_id\": 1,                 # Derived from '\"'\"'id'\"'\"' in input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.05582, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.055857, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",       # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.055888, "o", "> "]
[21.055919, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.055942, "o", "> "]
[21.055996, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02\",   # Formatted from '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"' in input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.056018, "o", "> "]
[21.05607, "o", "    \"role_count\": 2,              # Count of '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' from input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.056093, "o", "> "]
[21.05617, "o", "    \"primary_role\": \"admin\"       # If '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' is empty, this must be null (JSON null, not \"null\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.056193, "o", ">   },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.056216, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.056239, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.056262, "o", "**Requirements**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.056368, "o", "- You must use jq to perform this transformation. Using other programming languages (e.g., Python, Ruby) is strictly prohibited.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.056396, "o", "> "]
