[49.452572, "o", "ive_users_report.json\r\nsh /app/cmd.sh\r\ncmp /tmp/ref.json /app/active_users_report.json && echo cmd-sh-reproduces\r\nrm /app/active_users_report.json\r\njq $(yq -r '.args[]' /app/jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '.filter' /app/jq_args.yaml)\" /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json\r\ncmp /tmp/ref.json /app/active_users_report.json && echo yaml-reconstructs\r\nhead -c 120 /app/active_users_report.json; echo; tail -c 60 /app/active_users_report.json — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cp /app/active_users_report.json /tmp/ref.json rm /app/active_users_re…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 6 tool call(s) so far\r\nAll three deliverables are in place and verified:\r\n\r\n- **`/app/active_users_report.json`** — 346 active users (matches the 346 `\"status\": \"active\"` entries in the input), sorted ascending by `username`, 2-space indented. Verified: every `last_login` matches `^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$`, sort order is correct, all objects have exactly the six required keys, and the 50 users with empty `roles` have `role_count: 0`"]
[49.452668, "o", " and JSON `null` for `primary_role` (no `\"null\"` strings, no nulls where roles exist).\r\n- **`/app/cmd.sh`** — the exact jq command with output redirection; re-running it from scratch reproduces the report byte-for-byte (`cmp` clean).\r\n- **`/app/jq_args.yaml`** — `filter` holds the full jq expression; `args` is `[\"--indent 2\"]`. The documented reconstruction command `jq $(yq -r '.args[]' ...) \"$(yq -r '.filter' ...)\" /app/users.json > ...` was executed and also reproduces the report byte-for-byte.\r\n\r\nThe filter used:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[ .[] | select(.status == \"active\")\r\n  | { user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email,\r\n      last_login: (.last_login | split(\"T\")[0]),\r\n      role_count: (.roles | length),\r\n      primary_role: (if (.roles | length) > 0 then .roles[0] else null end) }\r\n] | sort_by(.username)\r\n```\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.8-flash-next tools=6 surface=b1d6c95da52f\r\n"]
